[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence"]
[Variation "Classical Variation"]
[ECO "C11"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "e5-pressure,c5-break"]

1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 { Develops a piece and defends e4, keeping options open. } 3... Nf6 { Attacks e4 and develops, keeping the Classical structure. }
4. Bg5 { Pins the knight on f6 against the queen. } ( 4. e5 Nfd7 5. f4 c5 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. Be3 Be7 8. Qd2 O-O ) 4... Be7 { Breaks the pin. }
5. e5 { Attacks the knight on f6. } ( 5. Bxf6 Bxf6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Bd3 dxe4 8. Nxe4 Be7 ) 5... Nfd7 { The knight steps back and now hits e5. }
6. Bxe7 { Trades the bishop that was pinning the knight. } 6... Qxe7 { Recaptures with the queen, so Black's pawns stay intact. }
7. f4 { Protects e5 with a pawn. } 7... O-O { Castles. The king is safe behind the f, g and h pawns. }
8. Nf3 { Develops and defends d4 and e5. } 8... c5 { Hits d4. The French needs this pawn break to undermine White's centre. [%cal Gc5d4] }
9. Qd2 Nc6 { Another attacker on d4. } 10. O-O-O a6 { Prepares ...b5 and a queenside attack, while the white king sits on the same side. } 11. dxc5 Nxc5 *
